# Only what a call gives comes round as `x`, and `x + 1` is no step of it: nothing says that it is an integer. Asked for an int32 in front of the loop, a start or a step with a fraction sent the whole loop into a copy built for size. Nothing is asked: `x` goes round as a number.
# RUN(WEIGHS): walk f4 mechanisms=all
# WEIGHS: number @Double) isInLoop=true isLoopHead=true
# RUN(UNASKED): walk f4 mechanisms=all
# UNASKED-NOT: testedType=i32
# A way round that brings `x` itself under a narrower name brings no step either.
# RUN(WAITS): walk f5 mechanisms=all
# WAITS-NOT: testedType=i32
# `at` is stepped on one way and brought by a call on the other: it is asked in front, so the other copy is built for size. It carries `at` raw, as a double; the typed build is left at the call all the same, for a copy that is dear: the builds are made again and the call stands in both.
# RUN(SCANS): walk f6 mechanisms=all
# SCANS: number @Double) frequency=Rare isLoopHead=true
# SCANS: = CallDirect {{*}} function=f3
# SCANS: i32 @Int32) isInLoop=true isLoopHead=true
# SCANS: = CallDirect {{*}} function=f3
# SCANS-NEXT: = TypeTest {{*}} testedType=i32
# Steps and starts with fractions, past every int32, texts, nothing, a big integer, NaN; the helper's other code lays another step.
